<div class="centered-article-text">
  <p>
    Adsum’s Spring/Summer 2019 collection is inspired by high performance yacht racing. It is not a retro or ironic look at it, but a real appreciation of the skill and precision of a technical outdoor sport. 
    <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0664/2387/files/collage2.jpg?17057588623632429460">
    <div class="blog-img-caption">SS19 collection inspiration.</div>
  <p>
    Radiant saturated colors like hi-vis yellow, safety orange, and bright blue reference the sportier race-day color palette of performance yacht competition and weave their way throughout the collection. These are balanced by the subdued hues of washed out yellow, rich green, and beige that capture the more casual land-based lifestyle behind the racing culture. 
  </p>
  	<img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0664/2387/files/adsum-sailing-casual-bigger3.jpg?4043478210497979518">
  	<div class="blog-img-caption">Sailing crew doing light pad work. / Team Brunel Volvo Ocean 65 race team mid embrace.</div>
      	<img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0664/2387/files/adsum-ss19-lookbook-514_1a745312-f5e5-4c25-b233-a3b2a0ed1f1a.jpg?17057588623632429460">
    	<div class="blog-img-caption">SS19 Hardshell Anorak shot in the Doyle Sail making loft on historic City Island, Bronx NY.</div>
  <p>
    Obvious yacht racing aesthetic cues on the hardshell Anoraks from SS19 can be seen in color block design. The reflective throat tab panel featured on the lightweight anorak gives the jacket a burst of color while adding practicality of high-power reflectivity. Choose the hardshell anorak for severe weather situations and the lightweight Anorak when packing practicality comes into play. Either one of our SS19 waterproof outerwear options will keep you dry for seasons to come. 
  </p>
